15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Stacked bar chart showing yearly cases treated with various immune checkpoint inhibitors from 2009 to 2025. Pembrolizumab and nivolumab cases increase substantially, peaking in 2024. Smaller contributions from atezolizumab, durvalumab, cemiplimab, and others are also shown in distinct colors. Specific drug counts per year are listed beneath the x-axis for reference.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Stacked bar chart showing the number of immunotherapy cases by sex, with separate bars for female, male, and not specified groups. Each bar is segmented by drug type, including Atezolizumab, Avelumab, Cemiplimab, Dostarlimab, Durvalumab, Ipilimumab, Nivolumab, Pembrolizumab, Tislelizumab, and Toripalimab, as indicated by the legend. Numerical totals are labeled atop each bar: 7,683 cases for females, 10,870 for males, and 1,761 not specified. Drug-specific case counts for each sex group are listed below the chart.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Heatmap-style table showing the number of case reports for various neurological adverse events associated with different immunotherapies, including durvalumab, nivolumab, atezolizumab, ipilimumab, avelumab, cemiplimab, dostarlimab, tremelimumab, and pembrolizumab. The table highlights that neuropathy peripheral, myasthenia gravis, taste disorder, encephalopathy, cerebral infarction, and brain edema have the highest case numbers, shown in dark red, particularly with pembrolizumab. Color scale on the right indicates case frequency from low \(white\) to high \(red\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Heatmap visualizing the reporting odds ratio \(ROR\) for various neurological disorders across seven medications, with higher RORs and confidence intervals highlighted in red, and a color bar indicating ROR: 95 percent confidence interval lower values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Heatmap illustrating the number of case reports for various neurological disorders associated with different immune checkpoint inhibitor drugs. Rows represent disorder categories and columns represent drugs, with color intensity indicating higher case counts. A color bar on the right provides a quantitative legend for case report frequency.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Heatmap chart showing reporting odds ratios for various neurological disorders versus different immune checkpoint inhibitors, with the highest values indicating increased risk of central nervous system infections and inflammations, especially for atezolizumab and nivolumab, highlighted in dark red.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
